<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <QuickAction> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
         matching parent xml file" error. It is also why there is no <description>: no quick
         action in this repo carries one (0 of 80 measured), QuickAction.Description is capped at
         255 characters, and a comment is repo-only and never sent to the Metadata API.

         ADDED 2026-08-26. User decision: "we don't need a quick action named 'Advance Stage';
         instead we need the NEXT STAGE NAME." One headless action PER DISPOSITION HOP, labelled
         with the stage the click lands on, replacing the single generic Advance Stage button on
         the DISPOSITION side of NDA__c. Same shape as the four Disposition__c.Advance_to_*
         actions built on 2026-08-19.

         🔴 THE LABEL IS THE ONLY THING THAT DIFFERS BETWEEN THESE ACTIONS. It points at the SAME
         c/advanceRecordStage bundle as NDA__c.Advance_Stage, and that component names no object
         and holds no stage map: RecordStageAdvanceService derives the target from the record's
         CURRENT stage via CONFIG_BY_TYPE, keyed per RECORD TYPE. So the label is a promise the
         page's visibility rule keeps, not an instruction the client sends - the LWC could not
         send a target if it wanted to (advance() takes only a recordId).

         ⇒ THE LABEL AND THE VISIBILITY RULE MUST BE KEPT IN STEP BY HAND. This action is placed
         on NDA_Record_Page under {!Record.Status__c} EQUAL 'Prepare', because
         NDA_DISPOSITION_NEXT_STAGE maps 'Prepare' => 'Approved'. If that map entry ever changes,
         this label lies and the rule must move with it. The server still refuses anything the map
         does not allow, so the failure mode is a mislabelled button, never a bad write.

         ACQUISITION IS UNTOUCHED. NDA__c.Advance_Stage still exists and still serves
         Acquisition_NDA (Pending -> Received -> Signed -> Sent); it is not deleted, renamed or
         re-pointed. -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>Approved</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>advanceRecordStage</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
